PATCH 584: extender op 0x50 -- the object projection (ba7d) -- and its two callers 2471/3eb3.

board:0002.  The depth sorter 2471 posts op 0x50 for every render node (3eb3: `lea si,[bx+0xa] ; mov
dx,[bx+6] ; call e189`), and 2908/290e post it for the effect record 0x6bbe.  The service (1266 =
`movzx esi,si ; add esi,[0xca1] ; call ba7d`) turns the node's world position into a screen position and
a depth row; ba7d was not in the decompile and the shim returned 0, so every node landed at (0,0) at
depth 0 and the model rasterizer (op 0x40) never drew a vehicle where it stands.  Transcribed from
0xba7d-0xbc05:

  ba7d   ba7b = the height byte [esi+9]; ba73 = dx << 22; ebx = x - 90cc (within +-0x80000), ebp =
         -(y - 90d0) (within +-0x40000), both << 12; lateral = hi(9100 * ebx) - hi(90fc * ebp), depth =
         -(hi(9100 * ebp) + hi(90fc * ebx)) (<= 0x1fffffff); the depth << 3 less ba73 (a negative
         difference is folded into ba73 and the depth becomes 0); the 0x4624 row table searched from
         the middle when past the middle row ([0x3a20] rows), the near row ba6f; depth + ba73 searched
         on, the far row ba6b; scale = 0x4224[row] >> 3 (0 fails); y = ((height - (90df >> 1)) as a
         signed byte << 18) / scale + 0x80, x = lateral / scale + 0x80, both within +-0x800.
         Returns AX = y, CX = x, EDX = the depth, ESI/EDI = the far/near rows; on failure AX = CX =
         0xfc18, EDX = -1, ESI = EDI = 0x32.
  3eb3   stores AX/CX/EDX/SI/DI into the node (+0x26/+0x28/+0x2a/+0x2e/+0x30) and returns CF =
         (EDX == -1); Ghidra took BX as a host pointer and stored the incoming registers.  2471's
         inline copy stored 0 for AX/CX and the cursor for DI.  The registers travel through the
         shim's op-0x50 lanes (g_fist_op50_*).

  Measured against the oracle's register trace of ba7d (scratch/oracle/regtrace_op50): on AZER1's
  first frame the four nodes the original projects successfully are the four the port projects, with
  the same x, the same depth and the same rows (43/0x769864e8/185-184, 297/0x53754350/157-156,
  196/0xc13a5c30/232-232, 54/0xce790ac8/240-239); y differs there only by the height byte the port's
  first frame has not yet set (board:0002's frame-1 pacing).  The fail/success pattern over the frame
  is the original's.

